invariant: INV-16
file: quic_token.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: the Retry token's tag is compared with memcmp instead of ct_memeq.
  memcmp returns at the first differing byte, so a client that can send
  Initial after Initial learns one tag byte per attempt and forges a token
  for its own address in 32 * 256 tries rather than 2^256. quic_token.h
  states that the comparison runs over all SHA256_LEN bytes for that reason.
  The answer stays correct, so no test sees it, which is why the rule and
  not bin/srv_quic_test is what catches it.

--- old
    uint32_t equal = ct_memeq(tag, want, SHA256_LEN);
--- new
    uint32_t equal = (uint32_t)(memcmp(tag, want, SHA256_LEN) == 0);
